{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8294732",
      "title": "Using useEffect for Handling (Some) Side Effects",
      "sourceHash": "5c4fa1204df7720d481355de446297a2b97ad04ceeb1adbc9745faf9ad972069",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 3.63,
          "en": "So, how can we use \"React useEffect Hook\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.63,
          "end": 5.61,
          "en": "to get rid of this problem?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.61,
          "end": 9.423,
          "en": "So, to handle this side effect in a better way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.95,
          "end": 13.26,
          "en": "Well, first of all, we have to import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 15.153,
          "en": "useEffect from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 18.96,
          "en": "And with it imported like all hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "this hook must be executed in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 23.913,
          "en": "in the app component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 29.58,
          "en": "Now, useEffect, unlike useState or useRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.58,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "does not return a value, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "Instead, useEffect needs two arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "And the first argument is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 42.573,
          "en": "that should wrap your side effect code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "So, in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 47.67,
          "en": "I'm creating an anonymous function and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.67,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "I move my location fetching state updating code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 54.3,
          "en": "into this anonymous function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.3,
          "end": 55.59,
          "en": "That's the first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 57.303,
          "en": "but that's not all we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "Instead, you should also pass second argument to useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "So, after this anonymous function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "and that second argument is an array of dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "of that effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 75.81,
          "en": "And I'll get back to these dependencies later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.81,
          "end": 78.423,
          "en": "For now, just add an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "Now, if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "if you change the code to look like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 87.63,
          "en": "You will not run into this infinite loop problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 89.163,
          "en": "And why is that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 93.03,
          "en": "Because the idea behind useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.03,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "is that this function which you pass as",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "a first argument to useEffect will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 104.28,
          "en": "by React after very important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "After every component execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "So, if the app starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "and the app component function executes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 116.37,
          "en": "this code here will not be executed right away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.37,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "Instead, it's only after the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 121.8,
          "en": "component function execution finished.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.8,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "So, after this JSX code here has been returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 127.98,
          "en": "That this side effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 132.12,
          "en": "you passed to useEffect will be executed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.12,
          "end": 134.28,
          "en": "So, React will execute that after",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.28,
          "end": 136.743,
          "en": "the component function is done executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.64,
          "en": "Now, if you then update the state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.64,
          "end": 144.18,
          "en": "the component function executes again as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.18,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "And in theory this effect function would execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 153.39,
          "en": "But that's where this dependencies array comes into play.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.39,
          "end": 156.57,
          "en": "If you define this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.57,
          "end": 159.54,
          "en": "So, if you do not omit it, but you define it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.54,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "Then, React will actually take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "at the dependencies specified there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "And it will only execute this effect function again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 172.65,
          "en": "If the dependency values changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.65,
          "end": 174.57,
          "en": "Now, this might sound a bit abstract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.57,
          "end": 176.57999999999998,
          "en": "but I'll show you a use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.57999999999998,
          "end": 179.883,
          "en": "Where we have a dependency a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 183.72,
          "en": "Here, where we have no dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 187.8,
          "en": "Those dependencies also can't change because we have none.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.8,
          "end": 190.41,
          "en": "So, they obviously never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.41,
          "end": 194.61,
          "en": "Therefore, React actually never re-executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.61,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "Instead, it only executes it once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 200.97,
          "en": "after this app component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.97,
          "end": 202.893,
          "en": "was executed for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 207.633,
          "en": "But then this effect function is never executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 211.17000000000002,
          "en": "If you would omit this dependencies array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.17000000000002,
          "end": 214.07999999999998,
          "en": "this effect function would be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.07999999999998,
          "end": 217.32,
          "en": "after every app component render cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 220.86,
          "en": "And therefore, we would still have an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.86,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "But with an empty dependencies array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 224.19299999999998,
          "en": "that will not be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "And therefore, with this out of the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 231.81,
          "en": "We will now set our available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.81,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "to the sorted available places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "Once we have to users' location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "without creating an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 242.25,
          "en": "And now, I'll just tweak the application a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.25,
          "end": 245.94,
          "en": "And down here on this places component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.94,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "I'll add the fallback text prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 252.27,
          "en": "which is supported by this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.27,
          "end": 257.27,
          "en": "and set it to Sorting places by distance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.64,
          "end": 261.18,
          "en": "Which is simply some fallback text that will be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.18,
          "end": 264.48,
          "en": "during the time where we don't have any places yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.48,
          "end": 267.363,
          "en": "Because we're still looking for the user's location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.35,
          "end": 272.04,
          "en": "Because initially of course, we don't have any places here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.04,
          "end": 273.753,
          "en": "We start with an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.25,
          "end": 278.01,
          "en": "With all that, If you save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "you should see a little pop-up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 283.383,
          "en": "that asks you for permission to get your location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.24,
          "end": 287.52,
          "en": "And if you click block, you'll break the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.52,
          "end": 289.17,
          "en": "So, here, I'll click allow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.17,
          "end": 291.33,
          "en": "And with that it'll fetch my location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.33,
          "end": 293.46,
          "en": "which can take some time as I mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.46,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "But then, it'll present me these places sorted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 299.523,
          "en": "by distance to my location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.36,
          "end": 303.09,
          "en": "Now of course, the order will depend on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.09,
          "end": 305.16,
          "en": "where you are located.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.16,
          "end": 308.97,
          "en": "For me, it looks pretty accurate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.97,
          "end": 311.94,
          "en": "I'd say, I haven't checked all locations here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.94,
          "end": 315.66,
          "en": "And it's just some dummy data anyways, but it looks correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.66,
          "end": 318.27,
          "en": "There also is no error in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.27,
          "end": 320.55,
          "en": "And therefore, this code now works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 320.55,
          "end": 323.13,
          "en": "And we're handling this side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 323.13,
          "end": 326.19,
          "en": "in a way that does not crash our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 326.19,
          "end": 329.133,
          "en": "Which I guess is always a good thing to have.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}